    <div class="alpheios-lex-entry" lemma-id="n43738" body-key=""><b><span class="alpheios-lex-la" lang="lat">septem-vĭri</span></b> ,
		ōrum (-virūm, <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil. 6,
			5, 14</span></i>), m.
		vir, <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b><i>a
				board</i> or <i>college of seven men</i>, <i>the septemvirs.</i>
		</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>I.</b> Of the epulones (v. epulo,
			2.), <i><span class="en">Tac.
				A. 3, 64</span></i>; sing. septemvir, <i><span class="en">Luc. 1,
			602</span></i>; <i><span class="en">Plin. Ep. 2, 11, 12</span></i>;
					<i><span class="en">Inscr. Orell.
			2365</span></i>.—</div>
        <div class="alpheios-lex-lex_sense alpheios-lex-lex_sense1"><b>II.</b> For dividing lands, <i><span class="en">Cic. Phil. 5, 7, 21</span></i>; <i><span class="en">6, 5,
			14</span></i>; sing., <i><span class="en">id. ib. 5,
				12, 33</span></i>; <i><span class="en">id. Att. 15, 19, 2</span></i>.</div>
    </div> <div class="alpheios-lex-footnotes en"> </div>
